Worker Design

- multi-tenant Zeebe workers in Spring Boot/Java on AWS.

- Workers poll jobs from multi-tenant Zeebe cluster, handling business logic like cross-account AWS calls (S3/Lambda/SQS/FIS). 

- Central monitoring account linked to source accounts for metrics/logs viewing/alarms.


Metrics 

- Implicit
- Collect execution time, success/fail/validation error automatically via Zeebe's JobWorkerMetrics built-in Micrometer-compatible metrics
- counters: activated/handled/failed 
- timers: duration
- gauge: available jobs
- Dimensions: tenant, jobType.
- Enable via Spring Boot's Micrometer StatsD exporter
- async publish: Micrometer StatsD -> CloudWatch Agent (retries/batching).
- No explicit code; auto-tagged with jobType/tenant.

Application Logs

- INFO/ERROR/TRACE levels to CloudWatch Logs
- Centralized monitoring via cross-account observability
- Explicit

Business Logs (Audit Logs)

- Capture inputs, outputs, remote calls/responses in JSON 
- uniqueId, tenant, timestamp, tag ("summary" or "detail").
- Maintain timestamp order, scale via async batching.
- worker sends a JSON payload via an async SDK call to Firehose, which then handles the batching (e.g., every 60 seconds or 5MB) before pushing to S3.
- S3 publish: partition by date/tenant/uniqueId (e.g., s3://bucket/{tenantId}/yyyy/MM/dd/{uniqueId}.json)
- S3 Configurable retention
- Non-blocking/timestamp order/Fault-tolerant (retry / shutdown flushes queue / scalable)
- capture (inputs/outputs) for all workers can be made implicit using Spring AOP
- @Before/@AfterReturning/@AfterThrowing
- MDC - uniqueId, tenant, input vars
- Retrieval by uniqueId+tenant
- Retrieval audits by tenant Day
- Retrieval by Date Range
- optionally intercepting remote calls rather than logging in worker method itself


Testing

Unit: Mock ZeebeClient/business logic (JUnit/Mockito). 
Integration: zeebe-process-test with embedded Zeebe, validate full flows, logs, metrics mocks.

